WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.988
Steps six and seven read the results.

2
00:00:02.988 --> 00:00:05.037
Each pillar owner reads their tab.

3
00:00:05.037 --> 00:00:08.768
Every test ends in one
of six statuses: passed,

4
00:00:08.768 --> 00:00:12.599
failed, investigate,
skipped, planned, or error.

5
00:00:12.599 --> 00:00:15.112
Investigate means a person needs to look,

6
00:00:15.112 --> 00:00:19.175
and skipped carries a reason, such
as not licensed or not connected.

7
00:00:19.175 --> 00:00:22.908
The kit records every result
twice: the tool's value,

8
00:00:22.908 --> 00:00:26.375
unchanged, and one of
seven normalized results.

9
00:00:26.375 --> 00:00:28.063
That's the rule in the title.

10
00:00:28.063 --> 00:00:31.737
A skipped test is not a failed
control, and it's not a pass.

11
00:00:31.737 --> 00:00:37.576
It goes in its own column, with its reason:
a licensing decision, or a run to fix.

12
00:00:37.576 --> 00:00:43.000
Investigate counts as a finding until a
recorded review confirms or dismisses it.

13
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.413
Two federal cases.

14
00:00:44.413 --> 00:00:47.593
Not dot gov domain
usually means the agency's

15
00:00:47.593 --> 00:00:50.601
dot gov domain isn't
verified in the tenant.

16
00:00:50.601 --> 00:00:55.902
And Learn says impersonation protection
isn't yet available in G C C High and D O D,

17
00:00:55.902 --> 00:00:59.900
so a failed impersonation test
there is a boundary finding.
